  "notes": [
    "Targets are computed at sol_mode='peak' without speculative decoding; speculative-decoding configs are listed in `not_modeled`.",
    "Configs that enable speculative decoding at runtime can measure above 100% of a non-speculative single-token decode roofline.",
    "Throughput fields `output_token_throughput_per_chip` and `total_token_throughput_per_chip` use the closed-loop formula C * OSL / (prefill_time_for_C_reqs + OSL * TPOT) / num_chips to match `vllm bench serve` output token throughput at concurrency C; `steady_state_decode_throughput_per_chip` reports B / TPOT / num_chips.",
    "Exported `sharding` records runtime vLLM TP/DP/EP flags; for GDN/KDA configs (`qwen3.5-397b`, `kimi-k3`), estimator `dimensions` maps onto the 2D (ep, tp) device mesh (`tp * ep == num_devices`, `dp = 1`) so `expert_shards = tp * ep` and `attn_dp_devices = ep`."
